==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|erthely}}, {{m|enm|erthlich}}, {{m|enm|ierðlich}}, from {{inh|en|ang|eorþlīċ}}, corresponding to {{suf|en|earth|ly|id2=adjectival}}. Cognate with {{cog|non|jarðligr|t=earthly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈəːθli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-earthly.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|earthlier}}

# Relating to the [[earth]] or this world, as opposed to heaven; [[terrestrial]].
#: '''''earthly''' joys''
#* {{RQ:KJV|Philippians|3|18|19|(For many walke, of whome I haue told you often, and now tell you euen weeping, that they are the enemies of the crosse of Christ: / Whose end is destruction, whose God is their belly, and whose glorie is in their shame, who minde '''earthly''' things.)}}
# {{lb|en|negative|informal}} {{non-gloss definition|Used for emphasis}}
#* {{quote-journal|en |author={{w|Robert B. Semple Jr.}} |date=April 4, 1971 |page=E1 |journal=The New York Times |url=https://www.nytimes.com/1971/04/04/archives/he-seems-suddenly-like-a-man-under-siege-nixon.html |title=The Nation |text=The pressures of politics and war seem remote on this lovely stretch of California coastline, but last week there was no '''earthly''' way to avoid them.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en |author=Michael Hitzlik |date=June 10, 2016 |journal=Los Angeles Times |url=https://www.latimes.com/business/hiltzik/la-fi-hiltzik-social-security-20160610-snap-story.html |title=Column: Congress continues its stealth assault on Social Security’s customer service  |text=In fiscal terms, there’s no '''earthly''' reason for Congress to be stingy with Social Security’s administrative budget.}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Made of earth; [[earthy]].
#: {{rfquotek|en|Holland}}

